From c8e1bfc92d9bfb582bdbdb30a4a7fbc673534d37 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ash Pera <ashley.pera@noaa.gov>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 12:24:55 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 26/29] satmedmfvdifq: apply surface fluxes to the host layer
 mass

The surface sources are applied with dt/(zi(2) - zi(1)) while the fluxes
were made kinematic with rho_a, so applied over reported minus 1 is the
non-hydrostatic dz deviation.

Apply them with dt*rho_a*g/del.

Measured (C96, 24 h): FV3_GFS_v16 suite water residual +2.6e-8 ->
-3.6e-16 kg/m2/day. In control_p8 the two forms are equal up to rounding
(24-h T rms 0.146 K, noise).

Part of a water-conservation project for UFS physics (NOAA GML / CIRES).

AI-assisted: written with Claude Opus 5.5; reviewed by author
---
 physics/PBL/SATMEDMF/satmedmfvdifq.F | 4 +++-
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/physics/PBL/SATMEDMF/satmedmfvdifq.F b/physics/PBL/SATMEDMF/satmedmfvdifq.F
index 0eff6545..84f7265b 100644
--- a/physics/PBL/SATMEDMF/satmedmfvdifq.F
+++ b/physics/PBL/SATMEDMF/satmedmfvdifq.F
@@ -735,7 +735,9 @@
       enddo
 !>  - Compute \f$\frac{\Delta t}{\Delta z}\f$ , \f$u_*\f$
       do i=1,im
-         dtdz1(i)  = dt2 / (zi(i,2)-zi(i,1))
+!  surface fluxes are kinematic with rho_a: apply them to the host layer mass del/g
+!  (rho_a*(zi(2)-zi(1)) differs from del/g by the nonhydrostatic dz)
+         dtdz1(i)  = dt2 * rho_a(i) * g / del(i,1)
       enddo
 !
       do i=1,im
